From: Banana <bananalinux@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] command: SAVE_STATE_AUTO, the quit-time state on request, for a sleep

Quick resume writes "<state>.auto" only when a game quits, so a handheld that sleeps with a game open and runs
out of battery overnight loses the session. bananad now asks for that same file just before it freezes the game.
RetroArch answers a stdin command with nothing, so the result goes to /run/banana/autosave ("ok" or "fail").
Neither the manual slot nor its number is touched.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [a specific handheld's sleep]
---
--- a/command.h
+++ b/command.h
@@ -427,6 +427,7 @@
 bool command_get_config_param(command_t *cmd, const char* arg);
 bool command_show_osd_msg(command_t *cmd, const char* arg);
 bool command_toggle_analog_dpad(command_t *cmd, const char* arg);
+bool command_save_state_auto(command_t *cmd, const char* arg);
 bool command_load_state_slot(command_t *cmd, const char* arg);
 bool command_play_replay_slot(command_t *cmd, const char* arg);
 bool command_seek_replay(command_t *cmd, const char *arg);
@@ -468,6 +469,7 @@
    { "LOAD_CORE", command_load_core, "<core path>"},
    { "AUDIO_REINIT", command_audio_reinit, "No argument"},
    { "TOGGLE_ANALOG_DPAD", command_toggle_analog_dpad, "No argument"},
+   { "SAVE_STATE_AUTO", command_save_state_auto, "No argument"},
 };
 
 static const struct cmd_map map[] = {
--- a/command.c
+++ b/command.c
@@ -804,6 +804,23 @@
    return true;
 }
 
+/* The same automatic state RetroArch writes when a game quits (the "<state>.auto" file Quick resume loads at the next
+ * start), written now: bananad sends this just before it freezes a game for a sleep, so a battery that dies overnight
+ * loses nothing. It leaves the manual slot and its number alone. RetroArch gives a stdin command no reply, so the
+ * answer is a file: /run/banana/autosave holds "ok" or "fail" once the state is on the card (bananad removes it first
+ * and polls it). A missing /run/banana just writes nothing. */
+bool command_save_state_auto(command_t *cmd, const char* arg)
+{
+   FILE *f;
+   bool ok = command_event_save_auto_state() > 0;
+   if ((f = fopen("/run/banana/autosave", "w")))
+   {
+      fputs(ok ? "ok\n" : "fail\n", f);
+      fclose(f);
+   }
+   return ok;
+}
+
